{
  "description": "Retain an architecture-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec. DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader) returns measured metrics and metric_definitions; diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis) explains those measurements and their limitations.",
  "motivation": "Use reproducible diagnostics to guide model improvements while preserving the four-category recommendation task and avoiding unsupported assumptions about unavailable reviews, item attributes, or simulator traits.",
  "implementation_notes": "Keep view.model bound to the trained nn.Module and adapt the compatibility methods when its architecture changes. Process batches shaped B × L, masking padding in every probe. Possible measurements include positive-versus-negative score margins, pairwise accuracy, embedding norms, and recommendation coverage. Use only available interaction histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for twenty real training users, five per category. Select trials using macro-average validation HR@10 under the pinned evaluator; diagnostic measurements are not substitutes for that score. Preserve dataset routing, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, GAGC_DATA_DIR, single-GPU execution, and matching predictor serialization. The effective default is SASREC_EPOCHS=200.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe:\n    init(view, device): retain trained view and device\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state; enter evaluation mode\n        with gradients disabled:\n            for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n                features = view.log2feats(sequence)\n                compute positive and negative scores through view.predict_score\n                aggregate supported measurements over valid, nonpadding positions\n            compute supported model and recommendation measurements\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: measured values, metric_definitions: definitions including masks, units, and sample counts}\n\nfunction diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    include measured metrics and their definitions\n    distinguish observations from hypotheses\n    identify unavailable evidence explicitly\n    request actionable hypotheses for validation through macro HR@10",
  "originality": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "Connects model diagnostics to a constrained recommendation improvement loop through a stable adapter.",
    "negative": "The description specifies an integration contract rather than a new recommendation algorithm or demonstrated diagnostic method."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Can support architecture comparisons and targeted experiments using consistent, auditable measurements.",
    "negative": "Diagnostic usefulness must be established empirically; favorable probe values need not improve validation HR@10."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces and batch structure are explicit, making an initial SASRec implementation straightforward.",
    "negative": "Architecture changes require careful feature alignment, masking, state restoration, and consistent inference serialization."
  }
}
